WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:06.569
A drone program may manage still imagery, video, thermal files, telemetry, flight logs, maps,

00:00:06.569 --> 00:00:09.341
models, inspection notes, annotations, and reports.

00:00:09.341 --> 00:00:15.348
Every product should remain linked to the mission, aircraft, sensor, time, location confidence,

00:00:15.348 --> 00:00:16.734
and responsible reviewer.

00:00:16.734 --> 00:00:21.817
Use consistent file names, mission identifiers, folder structures, and metadata rules.

00:00:21.817 --> 00:00:24.589
Preserve originals separately from processed outputs.

00:00:24.589 --> 00:00:28.748
Record transformations such as stitching, enhancement, redaction, annotation, conversion,

00:00:28.748 --> 00:00:30.134
or artificial-intelligence assistance.

00:00:30.134 --> 00:00:34.293
Storage design addresses capacity, performance, encryption, backup, recovery, retention,

00:00:34.293 --> 00:00:36.141
legal hold, and deletion.

00:00:36.141 --> 00:00:41.686
Exports and temporary working copies deserve the same protection as the central

00:00:41.686 --> 00:00:45.382
repository because they may contain equivalent sensitive data.

00:00:45.382 --> 00:00:51.389
G I S integration can connect observations to authorized maps and asset records.

00:00:51.389 --> 00:00:55.548
Position metadata should be validated when navigation anomalies occur.

00:00:55.548 --> 00:00:58.782
Dashboards should communicate coverage, status, findings, confidence,

00:00:58.782 --> 00:01:01.092
and gaps without overstating precision.

00:01:01.092 --> 00:01:05.251
Reporting workflows distinguish direct observation, automated output, analyst judgment,

00:01:05.251 --> 00:01:06.637
and specialist diagnosis.

00:01:06.637 --> 00:01:10.796
Quality review should check evidence references, privacy, accuracy, uncertainty,

00:01:10.796 --> 00:01:14.492
and whether the product answers the mission request.

00:01:14.492 --> 00:01:19.113
Protect sensitive imagery of people, property, facilities, infrastructure, and operations.

00:01:19.113 --> 00:01:22.809
Limit distribution to legitimate recipients, control public release,

00:01:22.809 --> 00:01:27.892
and retain only what policy, law, evidence, and operational need justify.

00:01:27.892 --> 00:01:32.975
Where evidence integrity matters, preserve collection and processing lineage: who captured,

00:01:32.975 --> 00:01:36.671
transferred, transformed, reviewed, approved, and exported each product.

00:01:36.671 --> 00:01:43.140
This supports correction and accountability without claiming that every operational image is forensic evidence.
